{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789315494,"nonce":"2B9EVuz173TD0DDUgM1d/BMq/aQ=","message":"Correction: align_callsite_ics already re-keyed the snapshot by destination value for the optimised MIR, so an inlined site's reorder was handled; what was actually wrong was the numbering itself. The bytecode gives a slot to Call and CallKnownFunc, never SuperCall, while every walker in the engine (the alignment, fill_ic_with_cha, known_call_sites, cold_loop_headers, the ceiling) counted Call and SuperCall, and the backends counted Call only after the devirt rewrite. In a body with a super call, every later call read its neighbour's entry: a getter devirtualised to the next getter's field, with a class guard that passes. Reproducer: tests/e2e.rs e2e_calls_after_a_super_call_keep_their_inline_caches (13700000 expected, the old build printed 7452120 and varied between runs).\n\nFix: MirFunction carries ic_sites (result value -\u003e bytecode slot), numbered from the authoritative MIR before the compile clone is transformed; the inliner carries entries onto the calls it clones; every walker and both backends look entries up by result value, and the positional alignment is gone.","files":null}]}